  "_comment": [
    "Pythia cost model defaults, one entry per venue, read by the Rust core (embedded at build time,",
    "overridable at runtime), by the TypeScript paper engine, and by the Python research lab.",
    "These numbers are DEFAULTS from public fee schedules and typical quoted spreads. They are a starting",
    "point to be calibrated from recorded data (realised slippage on Pythia's own fills, recorded books),",
    "not measurements. When the recorder has data, replace them here rather than in code.",
    "Units: every *Bps field is basis points (1 bp = 0.01 %). Fees are the lowest-volume retail tier.",
    "halfSpreadBps is per side: what a taker pays against the mid. impactCoeff is the extra cost in bps when",
    "an order's notional equals the top-of-book depth on the side it takes, scaled by sqrt(notional / depth)",
    "(the square-root law). defaultDepth is the top-of-book depth in quote currency (USD) assumed when no",
    "live book is available. minNotional is the smallest order the venue accepts, in USD, approximately.",
    "symbols overrides any field for one instrument, keyed by base asset (BTC) or ticker (AAPL).",
